From a8368becd79d8377535fd1ea4175ee005113a2ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:45:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/38] vrend: do not require EXT_texture_shadow_lod where the
 slot is a comparison

TGSI puts a shadow comparison value that does not fit the coordinate vector
into a second operand, and the emitter appends that operand to the same
buffer it uses for a LOD bias. Two forms therefore look biased although
nothing about them is: TGSI_OPCODE_TG4, where the slot holds the gather's
comparison value, and TGSI_OPCODE_TEX2 on TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY,
where it holds the lookup's. Both asked the host for EXT_texture_shadow_lod.

textureGather on a shadow sampler and texture(samplerCubeArrayShadow, vec4,
float) are both core GLSL; the extension exists to add the bias and
explicit-LOD forms that core leaves out, which TXB2 and TXL2 still ask for
because they append a real bias in .y after the comparison value in .x. A
desktop GL host has no reason to implement the extension - zink never sets
pipe_caps::texture_shadow_lod, so Mesa's GLSL compiler rejects the `require`
outright - and the generated shader then fails to compile. For the gather
that put the context into error, which on this host costs the rest of the
run rather than the one draw; for the cube-array lookup the draw is dropped
and the guest reads back the cleared surface, which is what all three shader
stages of dEQP-GL45-ES31.functional.shaders.opaque_type_indexing.sampler.*.
samplercubearrayshadow report. Compiling the emitted source against such a
host directly reproduces it: every stage compiles the lookup with no
extension line and every stage is rejected with "extension
`GL_EXT_texture_shadow_lod' unsupported in <stage> shader" when the line is
present.

Exclude both opcodes. A host that does advertise the extension is unaffected,
because the requirement was never what made either form work: the generated
call is the same either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_shader.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
index 83f8bad..d6045c1 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -3366,8 +3366,16 @@ static void translate_tex(struct dump_ctx *ctx,
 
    bool has_bias = strbuf_get_len (&bias_buf) != 0;
    bool has_offset = strbuf_get_len (&offset_buf) != 0;
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias
+   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias.
+   // TEX2 and TG4 are not among them: neither passes a bias, both carry the
+   // shadow comparison value that does not fit the coordinate in that same
+   // slot, and both forms - texture(samplerCubeArrayShadow, vec4, float) and
+   // textureGather on a shadow sampler - are core GLSL. Requiring the
+   // extension for them fails to compile on a host that has no reason to
+   // implement it.
    if (has_bias &&
+       inst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_TEX2 &&
+       inst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_TG4 &&
        (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY))
